      "description": "Watch Platense vs Union Santa Fe highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 25, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina witnessed a tense encounter on 2026-07-25 as Platense and Union Santa Fe locked horns in a match defined by high stakes and shifting momentum. Both sides entered the pitch with something to prove, setting the stage for a tactical battle that would keep fans guessing until the very end. Early Setback and Tactical Tension The match began with high intensity, but it was a moment of misfortune that broke the deadlock in the 24th minute. Tomas Fagioli inadvertently sent the ball into his own net, handing an early advantage to the opposition through an own goal. The first half continued to be a physical affair, with the referee busy brandishing yellow cards to keep the game under control. Brahian Cuello was the first to enter the book, followed by a flurry of cautions just before the break for Guido Mainero and Leonardo Heredia , reflecting the growing frustration and competitive edge on the pitch. The Second Half Surge and Penalty Drama As the second half commenced on 2026-07-25 , the atmosphere intensified even further. Juan Pablo Luduena received a caution early in the period but made amends in spectacular fashion later in the game. In the 72nd minute, Luduena found the back of the net to level the proceedings, sparking a chaotic and thrilling final quarter. However, the joy was short-lived for the home supporters as Union Santa Fe were awarded a penalty just minutes later. Cristian Alberto Tarragona stepped up with composure in the 79th minute, slotting the ball home from the spot to restore his side's lead. Merlini’s Moment and the Final Whistle With time running out, the managers turned to their benches to find a spark. In the 80th minute, Bautista Merlini was introduced into the fray, a substitution that would prove to be inspired. Just seven minutes after coming on, Merlini showcased clinical finishing to strike in the 87th minute, equalizing once more in a game that refused to settle. The closing minutes saw a flurry of tactical changes, including the introduction of Felipe Bussio and Mateo Peresutti , as both teams fought to secure a late winner, but the clock eventually ran out on a pulsating afternoon of football."
